# flag-coverage status - one line per codegen annotation flag.
# Format: <TClass>.<Field>  <qbe> <x86_64> <arm64>
#   a number = how many times that backend reads the flag
#   unused   = that backend deliberately never reads it
#
# A DROP below the recorded count fails the check: an arm was
# deleted, or a rename orphaned the flag.  A RISE is fine -
# refresh with --reset and commit alongside the change.
#
# A count is a SIGNAL, not a verdict.  Zero can be legitimate
# (the shape is handled through another route), and non-zero
# does not prove every path is covered - IsArrayAccess read 2
# in arm64 while its READ path was still missing.  See the
# header comment in FlagCoverage.pas.
#
# Regenerate with: flag-coverage --reset
#
# ---- arm64 zeros, triaged on-device 2026-07-26 (M1, macOS 15.7.7) ----
# All four arm64 zeros below were probed by writing the shape and compiling
# it.  NONE of them is a silent-wrong-code bug: one works through another
# route, and three are unimplemented features that fail LOUDLY with a
# NotYet at compile time, which is the honest failure mode.  Recorded here
# so the next person does not re-investigate them.
#
#   IsMethodCall      works.  O.Inner.Hi() lowers correctly on arm64 via
#                     another route (also confirmed on the Linux side).
#   IsInterfaceCall   shape is not CONSTRUCTIBLE on arm64 yet: storing an
#                     interface into a class field is itself
#                     'not yet lowered: store to a field of this type'.
#                     Interface calls through a LOCAL work (verified, 42).
#   IsClassVarRead    `static var` is unimplemented on arm64 — both the read
#                     ('not yet lowered: expression TFieldAccessExpr') and
#                     the write ('unresolved field assignment').
#   IsStaticPropGet   `static property` read likewise NotYet on arm64.
#
# These three stay at 0 until arm64 grows static members and interface
# fields; when it does, the count RISES, which the tool allows.  They are
# NOT marked `unused`, because they are gaps to be filled rather than
# deliberate non-use.

TFieldAccessExpr.FieldInfo                127  232  136
TFieldAccessExpr.IsConstant               4  7  15
TFieldAccessExpr.IsConstructorCall        4  6  9
TFieldAccessExpr.IsClassAccess            17  50  14
TFieldAccessExpr.IsImplicitSelf           19  57  31
TFieldAccessExpr.IsMethodCall             5  3  0
TFieldAccessExpr.IsInterfaceCall          5  1  0
TFieldAccessExpr.IsGlobal                 162  48  1
TFieldAccessExpr.IsClassNameAccess        1  1  2
TFieldAccessExpr.IsClassTypeAccess        1  1  1
TFieldAccessExpr.IsBuiltinToString        2  1  1
TFieldAccessExpr.IsVarParam               83  146  62
TFieldAccessExpr.PropIndexExpr            25  21  20
TFieldAccessExpr.IsCharAccess             3  1  1
TFieldAccessExpr.IsArrayAccess            8  11  3
TFieldAccessExpr.IsClassVarRead           4  4  0
TFieldAccessExpr.IsStaticPropGet          2  1  0
TMethodCallExpr.IsConstructorCall         4  6  9
TMethodCallExpr.IsMetaclassDispatch       3  4  2
TMethodCallExpr.IsStaticCall              3  4  5
TMethodCallExpr.IsGlobal                  162  48  1
TMethodCallExpr.IsVarParam                83  146  62
TMethodCallExpr.IsBuiltinToString         2  1  1
TMethodCallExpr.IsBuiltinInheritsFrom     1  1  1
TMethodCallExpr.IsProcFieldCall           5  5  1
